2931-## D244 · 2026-10-29 · Claude sets the dev/test split; scores are leads and Claude reads the traces every time; first the role-v29 baseline
2932-
2933-- Alex: "1. 好你来定 test validation split"; "2. 我觉得这是最容易出错的问题；你非常容易写死，我们在改的过程中如果drift你会一直用久的标准来衡量，这边需要有打分，但是“一定”要你自己下去看trace这是必须，记起来"; "3. v29 你先能跑出第一版的基线".
2934-- Decided: (1) the split is Claude's: the 118 bench articles, all seen, are the development set used for iterating and reading; a fresh test set from a later window no run has read is written from the text and frozen before its first send, and is scored once per configuration, never tuned on. (2) Every measurement has a score and Claude reads the traces: the raw answer beside the article, for every missed core or supporting entry and a sample of the extras and of the hits; a score is a lead, never the conclusion. The scorer hard-codes no rule of the standard: it reads the gold file it is given, prints the gold's and the page's sha256 and refuses a gold whose standard field names another page; a score is compared only with scores on the same gold; when the standard changes, the gold is re-derived and re-frozen before the next score. (3) The first task is the role-v29 baseline on the development set, three draws.
