     1	1. **Source for each rule in the three descriptions**
     2	
     3	   - **`speaker`:** “Who says it in this item: the outlet, the author or the person quoted” ([extraction.py:45](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:45)). Recording a speaker follows the [standard’s evidence-record rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:237). The closed list “the outlet, the author or the person quoted” is **unsourced** in the cited standard and decisions.
     4	   - **`original_who`:** “The party whose statement, figure or action it is” ([extraction.py:46](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:46)) partly follows “原始判断者” and D220’s “Original claimant” requirement ([standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:378); [D220](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2764)). Treating the subject of an action or figure as its original claimant is **unsourced**. The examples “the insurer” and “the regulator,” even when reported “without attribution,” apply that unsourced extension.
     5	   - **`original_who`:** “the outlet or author only for its own estimate, analysis or unnamed-source report” ([extraction.py:47](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:47)) has partial support for an author’s own estimate or analysis in “原始判断者” ([standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:378)). The exhaustive “only” restriction and assigning an unnamed-source report to the outlet or author as the original party are **unsourced**.
     6	   - **`original_day`:** “The day that party made it, as an ISO day when the item gives one” ([extraction.py:49](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:49)) follows the original statement-day requirement in [standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:385) and the ISO-day storage rule in [D203](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2604). The example “signed on 3 March 2026”: `2026-03-03` treats an action’s date as the statement day; that inference is **unsourced**.
     7	   - **`original_day`:** “empty when the item gives none or only a month” follows the unknown-day rule in [standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:385) and D203’s “keeps an ISO day and blanks anything else.”
     8	   - **`original_day`:** “the publication day only when the item is that party’s own release, filing, call or analysis” ([extraction.py:50](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:50)) is **unsourced** as a categorical restriction or exception. The standard says an *unknown original statement day* must not be filled with the reporting day; it does not make document type the test.
