1. **Source of each rule.** The descriptions preserve some rules from the standard, but also add rules about who originated an action and when to use a publication date.

   - **`speaker` — “Who says it in this item: the outlet, the author or the person quoted.”** Recording a speaker follows the standard’s “说话人” requirement. The closed list “the outlet, the author or the person quoted” is **unsourced** in the specified standard and decisions. [extraction.py:57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:57); [standard §2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:237).
   - **`original_who` — “The party that made the statement”** follows “原始判断者” and D220’s “Original claimant.” **“took the action or produced the figure, even when the item reports it without attribution”** is **unsourced** as a rule for identifying the original source. The insurer example applies that rule. [extraction.py:58](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:58); [standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:378); [D220](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2764).
   - **`original_who` — “an outlet that only relays it is not the original party”** follows the distinction between an original claimant and a relay. **“for a claim from unnamed sources, the unnamed source and the outlet that carried it”** preserves the unnamed source but is **unsourced** as a requirement to include the outlet: §5.4 says a relay is not always necessary. **“the outlet or author for its own estimate or analysis”** follows the original-claimant rule. [extraction.py:59](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:59); [standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:385); [D220](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2764).
   - **`original_day` — “The day that party made the statement, as an ISO day when the item gives one”** follows the original-statement-day rule and D203’s ISO-day requirement. The example **“announced on 3 March 2026”: `2026-03-03`** agrees when that is the original announcement date. **“or took the action”** is **unsourced** as an alternative to the statement day. [extraction.py:62](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:62); [standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:385); [D203](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2601).
   - **`original_day` — “empty when the item gives no day or only a month, never the publication day in place of an unknown day”** follows §5.4 and D203. **“A party’s own release, filing, call or analysis is dated its publication day”** is **unsourced** as an unconditional rule: the governing test is whether the original statement day is known. [extraction.py:63](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:63); [standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:385).

2. **Contradictions.**

   - **Action versus original statement.** “took the action” and “without attribution” make the actor the original party even when the article does not identify that actor as the source. The standard requires “原始判断者”; T7 asks for “the original source and statement day,” and T8 asks for “original attribution.” [extraction.py:58](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:58); [standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:378); [categories T7:29](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/categories-v54.json:29); [T8:33](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/categories-v54.json:33).
   - **Action day versus statement day.** “The day that party made the statement **or took the action**” can select a known action date when the original statement date is unknown. That conflicts with “原始发言日不知道就写不知道” and T7’s “statement day.” The announcement example itself does not show this conflict because it names an announcement. [extraction.py:62](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:62); [standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:385); [categories T7:29](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/categories-v54.json:29).
   - **Publication-day exception.** “A party’s own release, filing, call or analysis is dated its publication day” can conflict with “empty when the item gives no day” and “never the publication day in place of an unknown day” in the preceding sentence. An own analysis can repeat an earlier statement whose original day is unknown. [extraction.py:63](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:63); [standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:385).
   - **Role line 17 and category tiers.** No direct tier-rule contradiction found: the three descriptions assign attribution and date fields; [role-v54:17](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/role-v54.txt:17), [T7:28](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/categories-v54.json:28), and [T8:32](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/categories-v54.json:32) assign tiers. A correctly assigned tier can still accompany a misleading `original_who`.

3. **Company, industry or bench fitting.** None identified from the description text. “the insurer agreed to buy the broker” is industry-specific as an example, but its rule is not limited to insurance. The text alone does not establish whether that example came from a bench article. [extraction.py:58](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:58); [D237](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2874).

4. **Cases mislabelled or removed.**

   - A report says an insurer agreed to buy a broker but does not identify its source. “the insurer” as `original_who` can present the actor as the original source without evidence. The standard says invented source details are record errors. [extraction.py:58](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:58); [standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:385).
   - A transaction happened on a known date, but its original announcement date is unknown. “or took the action” can put the transaction date in the statement-day field. [extraction.py:62](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:62); [D203](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2601).
   - A company’s own analysis repeats an earlier statement without its date. “is dated its publication day” can replace the unknown original date with the analysis date. [extraction.py:64](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:64); [standard §5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:385).

   No description directly instructs the model to remove an evidence item.

5. **Ambiguities.**

   - “the outlet, the author or the person quoted” does not say which to enter when an author reports a quotation, or how to represent an organisation speaking. [extraction.py:57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:57).
   - “made the statement, took the action or produced the figure” gives no priority when those are different parties, or when the producer is unknown. [extraction.py:58](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:58).
   - “the unnamed source and the outlet that carried it” does not identify which outlet to use when an article relays another outlet’s unnamed-source report. [extraction.py:60](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:60).
   - “made the statement or took the action” gives no priority when both dates are known and differ. “A party’s own … analysis is dated its publication day” does not distinguish its own new analysis from an earlier statement it repeats. [extraction.py:62](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:62).

6. **Agreement with the signed golden set’s `who` convention.**

   - **`speaker`: partial agreement.** Its outlet, author and quoted-person choices cover some gold entries, but the gold’s single `who` field often combines original party and relay, such as **“Firmus (announced June 29, 2026; reported by SemiAnalysis)”**. The description does not specify how that combined convention maps to `speaker`. [extraction.py:57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:57); [gold:8059](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/golden-v3/golden-v3-signed.json:8059).
   - **`original_who`: partial agreement.** The unnamed-source wording agrees with **“an unnamed tech executive (to the Financial Times)”**. But the gold also identifies a publisher on another party’s action as **“Nebius (publisher), on LangChain’s release”**, and an unsourced report as **“the author (Jack Delaney); no source given”**. Those do not consistently follow the instruction to name the party that took the action as the original party. The gold’s `who` field combines roles, so it is not a one-to-one specification of this schema field. [extraction.py:58](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:58); [gold:14704](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/golden-v3/golden-v3-signed.json:14704); [gold:13645](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/golden-v3/golden-v3-signed.json:13645); [gold:12464](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/golden-v3/golden-v3-signed.json:12464).
   - **`original_day`: partial agreement, with a limit.** The Firmus entry includes a dated announcement, consistent with the announcement example. The `who` convention alone does not establish that an action date or an own publication date is always the original statement date. [extraction.py:62](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:62); [gold:8059](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/golden-v3/golden-v3-signed.json:8059).

7. **Resolution of the [version 53 review](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/fields-2026-10-30/review-v53.md).**

   - **Source findings:** the unsourced `speaker` list remains. The unsourced actor-as-original-source rule remains. The unnamed-source attribution changes from outlet/author to unnamed source plus outlet, resolving the identified loss of the unnamed source; requiring the outlet remains unsourced. ISO statement day and empty unknown/month remain supported. The action-date extension and unconditional own-publication exception remain unsourced.
   - **Contradictions:** the signing example is replaced with an announcement example, but the action-date conflict remains explicit in “took the action.” The restriction that could blank a *known* statement date equal to a news article’s publication date is removed. The actor-versus-original-source conflict remains, although the regulator example is removed. As in v53, no direct tier-rule contradiction was found.
   - **Fitting:** neither review identifies company- or bench-fitted wording from the text alone.
   - **Mislabelled cases:** the action-date and actor-as-source risks remain. The known-date-equal-to-publication-day omission is resolved. Neither version directly instructs removal of an item.
   - **Ambiguities:** the speaker choice remains unresolved. “produced the figure” clarifies one option but does not resolve competing parties. The action-versus-statement date is now explicit as two alternatives, without priority. The own-publication ambiguity remains and is now an unconditional sentence.
